+<p>This section runs the default SPLIT purification and visualizes
+purified data.</p>
+<div class="sourceCode" id="cb15"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb15-1"><a href="#cb15-1" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="co"># Run SPLIT purification</span></span>
+<span id="cb15-2"><a href="#cb15-2" tabindex="-1"></a>res_split <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> SPLIT<span class="sc">::</span><span class="fu">purify</span>(</span>
+<span id="cb15-3"><a href="#cb15-3" tabindex="-1"></a>  <span class="at">counts =</span> <span class="fu">GetAssayData</span>(xe, <span class="at">assay =</span> <span class="st">&#39;Xenium&#39;</span>, <span class="at">layer =</span> <span class="st">&#39;counts&#39;</span>), <span class="co"># or any gene x cells counts matrix</span></span>
+<span id="cb15-4"><a href="#cb15-4" tabindex="-1"></a>  <span class="at">rctd =</span> RCTD,</span>
+<span id="cb15-5"><a href="#cb15-5" tabindex="-1"></a>  <span class="at">DO_purify_singlets =</span> <span class="cn">TRUE</span> </span>
